["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The same patch of bush can be empty at noon and full at 4 pm. Time and weather move grouse as much as habitat does.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 430\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A 24 hour clock of a grouse day, hunter lore, 75 percent. About 6 to 9 am: feed and pick grit on edges and roads. About 9 am to 3 pm: rest and dust bathe. About 3 pm to dusk: feed again. Night: roost in trees or snow. Legal hunting hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset. Tip: at midday spruce and dusky grouse often sit in trees, which is your .22 time.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"430\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A grouse day (hunter lore, 75%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" r=\"130\" fill=\"#2f3a4a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L330.0 200.0 A130 130 0 1 1 74.4 166.4 Z\" fill=\"#fdf3d6\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L322.0 200.0 A122 122 0 0 1 286.3 286.3 Z\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L286.3 286.3 A122 122 0 0 1 113.7 286.3 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L113.7 286.3 A122 122 0 0 1 79.0 184.1 Z\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L79.0 184.1 A122 122 0 0 1 322.0 200.0 Z\" fill=\"#4a5a70\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" r=\"52\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"59.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Midnight</text>\n<text x=\"346.0\" y=\"205.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6 am</text>\n<text x=\"200.00000000000003\" y=\"351.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Noon</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"205.00000000000003\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6 pm</text>\n<text x=\"286.84467605606096\" y=\"240.97224264231843\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feed</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"299.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rest, dust</text>\n<text x=\"110.98856782746007\" y=\"235.2153097384972\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feed</text>\n<text x=\"206.14789414763345\" y=\"111.20126121557128\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Roost</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">24 hours</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"384\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Morning feed includes grit on road edges.</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"402\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Legal: 1 h before sunrise to 1 h after sunset.</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Midday: spruce, dusky often sit in trees (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Feed early and late, rest midday, roost at night (hunter lore, 75%).</li><li>Legal: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the day, with the evidence level for each claim</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Feed early morning and late afternoon</td><td>Agency and hunter accounts</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>Pick grit and dust on road edges</td><td>Agency accounts, sign</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>Rest and dust bathe midday</td><td>Hunter accounts</td><td>70%</td></tr><tr><td>Spruce and dusky sit in trees midday</td><td>Hunter accounts</td><td>65%</td></tr><tr><td>Roost in trees, ground or snow at night</td><td>Agency accounts</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>Adults move only a few hundred metres a day</td><td>Pennsylvania Game Commission</td><td>75%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Hours rule: \"To hunt game, except migratory game birds from one hour after sunset to one hour before sunrise\" is unlawful (99%, item 38, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/13\">Rule Book</a>).</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grass-fir-edge.jpg\" alt=\"Grass and fir edge: morning feeding ground.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Grass and fir edge: morning feeding ground. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Andres Alvarado, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_colorful_of_Lac_Du_Bois_Grasslands.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-snowberry.jpg\" alt=\"Snowberry: a fall and winter food.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snowberry: a fall and winter food. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: NPS Photo, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:File-Symphoricarpos_albus_-_native;-Blooms_June_-_July;_(9352ce2f-155d-4519-3e7c-5033029f6900).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>First light to mid morning: edges, trails, road shoulders <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>They need grit for the gizzard <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: morning detail</summary><ul><li>Grouse pick small gravel to grind food in the gizzard <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Road edges and trails supply it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Young birds in September and October feed on clover and berries along road edges and cut blocks (65 to 75%).</li><li>Sharp tailed grouse use roadsides and landings with clover, dandelion and yarrow heavily in fall (85%, BC species account).</li><li>Roads are also where the rules bite. See <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09/6\">How to hunt</a> before you hunt a road edge.</li><li>Tip: walk an old closed road or a trail away from traffic at first light.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 310\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A conifer with a dark spruce grouse sitting on a branch close to the trunk, circled. It looks like a dark blob near the trunk with the tail hanging down. Tip: look up slowly; midday is the time.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spot a grouse sitting in a tree</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"260\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"190\" y=\"40\" width=\"16\" height=\"225\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 70 L138 100 M198 70 L258 100\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 110 L108 140 M198 110 L288 140\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 150 L78 180 M198 150 L318 180\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 190 L48 220 M198 190 L348 220\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 230 L28 260 M198 230 L368 260\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(232 132) scale(0.8 0.8)\"><polygon points=\"-22,-4 -36,-8 -36,4 -22,6\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#3d3a35\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#3d3a35\"/><path d=\"M18 -20 q5 -5 10 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c23b22\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M216 140 l-6 20\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n<circle cx=\"232\" cy=\"132\" r=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"280\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">A dark blob</text>\n<text x=\"280\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">near the trunk</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tail hangs down. Look up, slowly.</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"301\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Midday is the time (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Birds loaf in cover and dust bathe <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The best time to still hunt sitters with the .22 (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: midday detail</summary><ul><li>Dust bathing: shallow bowls in dry dirt on road edges and banks, used to clean feathers <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Spruce grouse spend fall and winter days up in conifers (80%, Washington Department of Fish and Wildlife, earlier lesson).</li><li>Dusky grouse sit in big Douglas fir (Tip).</li><li>Tip: slow down at midday; look up, not ahead.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of thermals on a slope. Morning: the sun rises and warms the slope, warm air rises, and scent drifts uphill, so approach from above or the side. Evening: the sun sets, the slope cools, cool air sinks, and scent drifts downhill, so hunt from below or the side and leave before cold air drains your scent down to bedded deer.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dbe7f3\"/>\n  <circle r=\"18\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" cx=\"40\" cy=\"250\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"250;70;70;250\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.6;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"40;80;330;370\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.6;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <animate attributeName=\"fill\" values=\"#f3d36b;#f3d36b;#f2a56b;#e8590c\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;0.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n  </circle>\n  <path d=\"M0 290 L0 260 Q150 240 260 120 Q300 80 400 60 L400 290 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(220 160)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-14\" cy=\"-7\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.1;0.5;0.55;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 250 Q150 220 200 175 m-14 2 l14 -2 l-2 14\"/>\n    <path d=\"M150 260 Q220 210 270 140 m-14 2 l14 -2 l-2 14\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.6;0.65;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M270 120 Q220 190 160 235 m2 -14 l-2 14 l14 0\"/>\n    <path d=\"M330 100 Q280 170 230 215 m2 -14 l-2 14 l14 0\"/>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: warm air, scent goes UP\n    <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Evening: cool air, scent sinks DOWN\n    <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.05;0.9;1\" begin=\"1.5s\" dur=\"3.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"96\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You: above</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"262\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">You: below</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Thermals: up in the morning, down in the evening. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Last 2 hours of light: birds feed again (hunter lore, 70%).</li><li>Legal light ends 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: evening detail</summary><ul><li>Late afternoon feeding mirrors the morning: edges, berries, clover, buds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>In bitter cold, some hunters see birds feed in the warmest hours, about 1 to 4 pm (hunter account, 50%: Tip).</li><li>Roost: in trees (often conifers), on the ground, or under soft snow <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Thermals sink in the evening, so a dog working uphill gets scent from above (Tip).</li><li>Shooting light fades fast in timber; your watch says legal, the woods may say no (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 400\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Six weather tiles. Strong wind: birds are wild and flush far, hunt sheltered draws, hunter lore. Rain: birds sit under thick conifers to stay dry, hunter lore. Fresh snow: read tracks and roosts; birds dive into soft snow 20 centimetres or deeper, 75 percent. Bitter cold: feeding may shift to midday, hunter lore. Pressure front: no grouse study found, watch and log it. Moon: no grouse study found, do not plan around it.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"400\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Weather: where to look</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"108\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Strong wind</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Birds wild, flush far.</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hunt sheltered draws.</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hunter lore (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"108\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rain</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Under thick conifers.</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Birds stay dry there.</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hunter lore (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"156\" width=\"185\" height=\"108\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Fresh snow</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Tracks and roosts.</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Birds dive into soft</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">snow 20 cm+ (75%)</text>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"156\" width=\"185\" height=\"108\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bitter cold</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Feeding may shift</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">to midday.</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hunter lore (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"272\" width=\"185\" height=\"108\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#9aa0a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pressure front</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"322\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">No grouse study</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">found. Watch and</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"358\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">log it (Journal).</text>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"272\" width=\"185\" height=\"108\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#9aa0a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Moon</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"322\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">No grouse study</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">found. Do not plan</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"358\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">around it.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Wind and rain move birds into shelter (hunter lore, 55 to 60%: Tip).</li><li>No grouse study found on pressure fronts or the moon.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: each weather type, with evidence</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Weather</th><th>What birds do</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Strong wind</td><td>Wild, flush early; shelter in low, thick cover</td><td>Hunter lore (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Rain</td><td>Under middle aged conifers</td><td>Hunter lore (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Calm overcast</td><td>Moving and feeding; good hunting</td><td>Hunter lore (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Fresh soft snow</td><td>Snow roosts; tracks show everything</td><td>70 to 75%</td></tr><tr><td>Crust, deep cold</td><td>Into thick conifers; weight loss</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>Falling pressure, cold front</td><td>No grouse study found</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td></tr><tr><td>Moon phase</td><td>No grouse study found</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Hunting magazine and blog advice says calm overcast days are best and windy days make grouse skittish (55 to 60%).</li><li>Keep your own record in the Journal: date, weather, flushes. Your data beats lore (Tip).</li><li>See also <a href=\"#/s/weather-moon\">Weather and the moon</a> for deer.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of an open road with a shaded band 200 metres each side. In a Pennsylvania study, birds within about 200 metres of open roads were shot more often; more birds lived past 200 metres. Walk past the road band.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Walk past the shot birds</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"150\" width=\"400\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"100\" width=\"400\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".15\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"172\" width=\"400\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".15\"/>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Open road</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">0 to 200 m: shot most</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Past 200 m: more birds live</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(60 125) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(300 200) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(120 60) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(230 280) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(350 60) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(330 284) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Birds close to open roads get shot more <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Walk past 200 m from the road (Tip, based on the study).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: detail</summary><ul><li>Pennsylvania: 48% harvest rate near open roads versus 19% farther away; male survival 23% within 201 m of roads versus 36% beyond <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Opening weekend and the first snow bring the most hunters (Tip).</li><li>Weekday mornings on gated roads see the least traffic (Tip).</li><li>The flip side: birds far from roads are less shot, not less wary (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 430\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A 24 hour clock of a grouse day, hunter lore, 75 percent. About 6 to 9 am: feed and pick grit on edges and roads. About 9 am to 3 pm: rest and dust bathe. About 3 pm to dusk: feed again. Night: roost in trees or snow. Legal hunting hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset. Tip: at midday spruce and dusky grouse often sit in trees, which is your .22 time.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"430\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A grouse day (hunter lore, 75%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" r=\"130\" fill=\"#2f3a4a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L330.0 200.0 A130 130 0 1 1 74.4 166.4 Z\" fill=\"#fdf3d6\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L322.0 200.0 A122 122 0 0 1 286.3 286.3 Z\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L286.3 286.3 A122 122 0 0 1 113.7 286.3 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L113.7 286.3 A122 122 0 0 1 79.0 184.1 Z\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 200 L79.0 184.1 A122 122 0 0 1 322.0 200.0 Z\" fill=\"#4a5a70\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" r=\"52\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"59.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Midnight</text>\n<text x=\"346.0\" y=\"205.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6 am</text>\n<text x=\"200.00000000000003\" y=\"351.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Noon</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"205.00000000000003\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6 pm</text>\n<text x=\"286.84467605606096\" y=\"240.97224264231843\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feed</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"299.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rest, dust</text>\n<text x=\"110.98856782746007\" y=\"235.2153097384972\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feed</text>\n<text x=\"206.14789414763345\" y=\"111.20126121557128\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Roost</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">24 hours</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"384\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Morning feed includes grit on road edges.</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"402\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Legal: 1 h before sunrise to 1 h after sunset.</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Midday: spruce, dusky often sit in trees (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Rhyme: \"Gravel at dawn, dust at noon, berries at dusk, roost by the moon.\"</li><li>Number trick: \"1 and 1\": 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset.</li><li>Old hand's rule (tradition): \"Wind day, low and thick. Rain day, under the firs.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Look up at noon.\"</li><li>\"200 m past the road.\"</li><li>\"No study on the moon\": do not plan around it.</li><li>Rhymes are made for this course; the wind and rain rules are common hunter advice, not science.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Rule Book, Pennsylvania Game Commission, Hinterland Who's Who, BC species account, hunting writers. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source</summary><ul><li>Rule Book: <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/13\">hunting hours</a>, synopsis 2 October 2026 edition, page 11, items 37 and 38 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.pa.gov/agencies/pgc/wildlife/discover-pa-wildlife/ruffed-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pennsylvania Game Commission, Ruffed grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/en/wildlife/birds/ruffed-grouse.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hinterland Who's Who, Ruffed grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/frpa/iwms/documents/Birds/b_columbiansharptailedgrouse.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC species account, Columbian Sharp tailed Grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://projectupland.com/grouse-species/ruffed-grouse/hunting-ruffed-grouse-in-the-rain/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Project Upland, Hunting ruffed grouse in the rain</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Weather and upland hunting blogs and Ruffed Grouse Society winter strategies, search preview (50 to 55%, Tip only).</li><li>Washington Department of Fish and Wildlife, spruce grouse, read 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>All checked 2026-10-11 unless noted. Full log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-grouse.md</code>.</li></ul></details>"]